<section class="fragment-consult" data-artifact="plan" data-slice="realism-tuning">
  <p><strong>Panel of 1</strong> (codex, repo-aware). This is one opinion, not a consensus.</p>
  <p><strong>Verdict:</strong> Revise before implementation. The plan named the conflicts but ran the feasibility checks late.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Gating ball in play in the tempo phase conflicts with the evidence. Tempo, contest, fouls and corners need joint rounds.</li>
    <li>The corner source has no proof of enough events. The existing cross clearance aims away from goal. Count the eligible events and the yield first.</li>
    <li>4-1-2-1-2 must rise and 3-4-3 must fall. A shared scoring change cannot do both. Test this before tuning.</li>
    <li>Goals that rise in proportion leave the red-card cap ratio unchanged. The xG coefficients do not drive saves.</li>
    <li>The CLI pairing runs use other fixtures than the formations test. Screen on the test's own fixtures. Enforce the 0.08 floor on the sending-off share.</li>
    <li>The stop rule had no budget.</li>
  </ul>
  <p><strong>Taken into the plan:</strong> all six points, as steps 1 and 5–11.</p>
</section>
